From d687c6983a404156c540aca9f535c775217852e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:52:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GX front end: a display list's primitives fused into one draw
 (the GX worker and Smooth Motion's matching per draw, at a tenth of the
 draws)

Nine draws in ten at Forest Haven follow the draw before with no state
between them: the strips of one display list. Each was planned (state,
pipeline, textures, vertices), submitted and matched for Smooth Motion apart,
only to be batched with its neighbours at the end, about 21,000 draws a game
frame.

Now GxCoreSink asks the consuming sink to fuse such a primitive onto the draw
before when: triangles follow triangles, the vertex descriptor indexes
positions (not a particle's, a 2D sprite's or a wake's own), no draw scope or
draw tag is under way, and together they have at most 1,024 vertices
(frame_interp's kMaxBlendedVertices, so a mesh the game moves vertex by vertex
stays one Smooth Motion blends). The consumer also requires that nothing but
the draw's array spans came between them (no texture, TLUT or copy), and the
same vertex format and transform version. A fused draw keeps its primitives
(ConsumedDraw::segments) and gets the triangle indices they had apart,
rebased, and the union of their array spans. DOL_GX_FUSE=0 turns it off; the
shutdown line gives the draws fused.

Over an Outset run, 8.8 million draws became 0.87 million. Smooth Motion at
60, all of the i9's cores, CPU per game frame: GX worker 16.4 -> 7.1 ms at
Forest Haven, 11.4 -> 4.5 at Hyrule, 14.2 -> 5.1 in Hyrule Castle's room;
the in-between frames' matching 14.5 -> 2.9, 9.9 -> 0.9 and 12.4 -> 0.8; the
render worker 20-35 percent less. On four E-cores the game holds 30 frames a
second at every place tried (27-29 before at Outset, Forest Haven and Dragon
Roost) with in-between frames on (the pacer had turned them off at the sea,
Hyrule and Hyrule Castle).

Real frames are identical in Smooth Motion dumps at Outset, the sea by the
Forsaken Fortress, Forest Haven, Dragon Roost, Hyrule, the Forbidden Woods,
the Earth Temple's boss and three lava save states. In-between frames are
identical or differ at a few pixels' edges (a fused group's matrix rows and
motion samples are judged together); in Hyrule Castle's room and at the
Earth Temple's boss they are now drawn where the matching had taken the
frames for camera cuts and left them out. gxcore_tests' new draw fusion test
checks the fused plan against the two draws apart.
